To hide a block of text in HTML, you can use the CSS display property. Here are the steps:

1. Wrap the text that you want to hide within a <div> tag. For example:

<div class="hidden-text">This is the text I want to hide.</div>

2. In your CSS file, create a new style rule for the .hidden-text class and set the display property to none. This will make the text invisible on the page:

.hidden-text {
display: none;
}

3. Save your changes

To terminate a C program, you can use the exit() function. This function takes an integer argument that represents the exit status of your program. The value 0 indicates successful termination, while any other non-zero value indicates unsuccessful termination. Here's an example code snippet to demonstrate how to use the exit() function in C:

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("Hello, world!\n");
    exit(0); // Terminate the program with success (exit status 0)
